		prior: "You can add and scale. The dot product turns two lists into one number.",
		see: "Two arrows. Same direction, the product is large. Near a right angle, it is near 0.",
		plain: "The dot product is one number. It is large when the lists share a direction and are long.",
		situation: "Example: (2, 3) · (4, 1) = 8 + 3 = 11. (1, 0) · (0, 1) = 0: the two axes do not share a direction.",
